speechtext:
They did it to perfection in connection with the registration which took place some time ago, and not only did they do it then but they are ready to do it at any time in order to help Canada through this difficult period. Partisanship has been displayed to a degree in my riding, but we can overlook that. There is something more important to-day than the little odd display of partisanship in the taking of the census. Any hon. member who to-day had the privilege of listening to the words that emanated from the United Kingdom would feel disposed, I should think, to sit in silence in his place to-night and allow this work to ^proceed and the estimates to go through without holding up the session. The Minister of Pensions and National Health says "Hear, hear" in that regard. Let me ask this chamber to absolve me from any attempt to hold up the proceedings of this session at any time. I do not, however, wish the record to go out with the suggestion that there has been a pure, undefiled sheet, so far as the conduct of this particular vote is concerned, in the area from which I come. Quite true, they said, "We will take one or two of your nominations". They have three of mine-three nominations out of some hundred odd; and when more were suggested they said, "Oh, we must take care of those who are assigned to us from the churches, those who are assigned to us from the returned soldiers, those who are recommended to us from the schools, the schoolteachers-yes, provided they have the right kind of stripe-and we must take care of those who belong to what is known in my constituency as the Liberal association of Danforth." All these must be looked after; and when these are all taken care of, the member for Danforth may make one or two nominations-make a dozen and get one or two appointed.
I have no complaint. Go to it; get the census over this year. That is your policy;

take the responsibility for spending S3,000,090. I say it is wrong. The excuses which the minister has given for spending the money are not sound. The representations he has made on the floor of the house that, so far as possible, he has tried to be fair and has done it just as it was done ten years previously-
